item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yeon-namsaeng"><span class="enc-name">Yeon Namsaeng</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yeon Namsaeng was the eldest son of the Goguryeo military dictator Yeon Gaesomun and succeeded him as the kingdom's chief minister.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yeondeunghoe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yeondeunghoe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yeondeunghoe</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Yeondeunghoe is a Korean Buddhist lantern festival.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/yeongjo-of-joseon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yeongjo-of-joseon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Yeongjo of Joseon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yeongjo was the 21st king of Joseon Korea, ruling from 1724 to 1776, the longest reign of the dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/yeongnyu-of-goguryeo"><span class="enc-name">Yeongnyu of Goguryeo</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Yeongnyu of Goguryeo was the twenty-seventh king of Goguryeo, reigning from 618 to 642.</span></a></li></ul>
